# Wayland libdecor's system GTK/Pango plugin retains Fontconfig process-global
# font caches after SDL_Quit. Observed on Ubuntu 26.04, both when GTK init fails
# (320 bytes) and succeeds (font enumeration caches). No engine/SDL/Vulkan
# allocations are suppressed. Keep ASan/UBSan and all other leak checks enabled.
leak:libfontconfig.so.1
# The same system plugin intermittently leaks one 96-byte wl_proxy that it creates
# in libdecor_frame_commit (about 1 in 3 native Wayland runs; never under X11/CI).
# Matches only frames inside the plugin; SDL's own Wayland code is not suppressed.
leak:libdecor-gtk.so
